<title>USA: FP&amp;L Turkey Point 3 nuke at 56 pct output.</title>
<headline>FP&amp;L Turkey Point 3 nuke at 56 pct output.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Florida Power &amp; Light Co's 666 Megawatt (MW) Turkey Point 3 nuclear power plant has throttled production back to 56 percent of capacity, the Nuclear Regulatory Commission (NRC) said Friday.</p>
<p>The commission said the reduction was needed to correct a leak on the unit's main feedwater pump casing.</p>
<p>The plant, at Florida City, Fla., was operating at full capacity early Thursday.</p>
<p>The other unit at the facility, Turkey Point 4, was operating at its full 666 MW capacity, the NRC said.</p>
<p>Florida Power &amp; Light is a subsidiary of the FPL Group.</p>
<p>((--New York Power Desk + 212 859 1621))</p>
